{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1772836376453,"sessionID":"ses_33ab7ce6dffe91mo0SFnDFuC21","part":{"id":"prt_cc5484d980019pHpXiIKkHX0zq","sessionID":"ses_33ab7ce6dffe91mo0SFnDFuC21","messageID":"msg_cc54832b2001wF7C6DkdxSXfiU","type":"tool","callID":"call_function_dcbl508ymzxb_1","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/paule/MAD/.tmp/add-ability-to-create-new-ideas-from-the-server-view.instructions"},"output":"<path>/home/paule/MAD/.tmp/add-ability-to-create-new-ideas-from-the-server-view.instructions</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>1: You are an implementer breaking down a feature plan into concrete coding tasks.\n2: \n3: Feature: Add ability to create new ideas from the server view\n4: \n5: Plan:\n6: ## Plan: Add ability to create new ideas from the server web app\n7: \n8: ### Overview\n9: Add a \"New Idea\" form to the web app that sends a WebSocket message to a connected pipeline client, which then creates the idea locally using `FeatureFile.create()`.\n10: \n11: ### Architecture Flow\n12: 1. **Web UI** (index.html / client.html) → User fills in title, board, description\n13: 2. **Server** (api.go) → New REST endpoint `POST /api/clients/{id}/ideas` receives the request\n14: 3. **Server** (hub.go) → Forwards a `create_idea` WebSocket message to the connected pipeline client\n15: 4. **Pipeline client** (server_client.py) → Receives `create_idea` message, calls `FeatureFile.create()`\n16: 5. **Pipeline client** → Next state push reflects the new idea in the ideas stage\n17: \n18: ### Implementation Steps\n19: \n20: #### 1. Server: Add `create_idea` WebSocket message type (hub.go)\n21: - No changes needed in hub.go message handling — the server just forwards the message to the client via `SendToClient()`. The server doesn't need to understand the message content.\n22: \n23: #### 2. Server: Add REST endpoint `POST /api/clients/{id}/ideas` (api.go)\n24: - Add a new handler `serveCreateIdea` similar to `serveSubmitAnswers`\n25: - Accept JSON body: `{\"title\": \"...\", \"board\": \"...\", \"description\": \"...\"}`\n26: - Validate: client exists and is connected, title is non-empty, board is non-empty\n27: - Send `create_idea` WebSocket message to the pipeline client: `{\"type\": \"create_idea\", \"title\": \"...\", \"board\": \"...\", \"description\": \"...\"}`\n28: - Return 200 OK on success\n29: - Wire up routing in the existing `apiClientsHandler` by matching the `ideas` sub-path under a client ID\n30: \n31: #### 3. Pipeline client: Handle `create_idea` message (server_client.py)\n32: - In `_handle_incoming`, add a case for `msg_type == \"create_idea\"`\n33: - Add a new callback `on_idea_created` to the constructor (similar to `on_answers_received`)\n34: - Extract `title`, `board`, `description` from the message\n35: - Call the callback which will invoke `FeatureFile.create(board, title, description)`\n36: \n37: #### 4. Pipeline runner: Wire up the callback (runner.py)\n38: - When constructing `ServerClient`, pass an `on_idea_created` callback\n39: - The callback creates the idea via `FeatureFile.create()` and triggers a state push so the web UI updates immediately\n40: \n41: #### 5. Web UI: Add \"New Idea\" button and form (client.html)\n42: - Add a \"+\" button near the features header or in the ideas stage section\n43: - On click, show a simple inline form or modal with fields: Title (required), Board (dropdown from known boards, or text input), Description (textarea, optional)\n44: - On submit, POST to `/api/clients/{clientID}/ideas?key=...` with the JSON body\n45: - Show success/error feedback\n46: - The next poll cycle (5s) will show the new idea in the ideas stage\n47: \n48: #### 6. Web UI: Add to index.html aggregate view (optional)\n49: - Add a \"New Idea\" button to the dashboard's aggregate view\n50: - If multiple clients are connected, require selecting which client should create the idea\n51: - If only one client is connected, default to that client\n52: \n53: ### Files Modified\n54: - `server/api.go` — New endpoint and route wiring\n55: - `server/hub.go` — No changes needed (reuses existing SendToClient)\n56: - `server/templates/client.html` — New Idea UI form\n57: - `server/templates/index.html` — Optional: New Idea button in aggregate view\n58: - `pipeline/server_client.py` — Handle `create_idea` message type, new callback\n59: - `pipeline/runner.py` — Wire up the `on_idea_created` callback\n60: \n61: ### Edge Cases\n62: - Client disconnects between form submission and idea creation → Server returns error (client not connected)\n63: - Duplicate title → `FeatureFile.create` will use the same slug, potentially overwriting. Could add a check or append a suffix — but the existing `create` method already generates a unique ID so the JSON content differs. The slug-based filename could collide though, so we should handle this gracefully.\n64: - Empty or invalid board name → Validate on server side before forwarding\n65: - Board doesn't exist on client → The `FeatureFile.create` method creates the directory if needed, so this is safe\n66: \n67: Write a detailed implementation spec — a list of specific coding tasks.\n68: For each task: what to create or modify, the approach, and dependencies on other tasks.\n69: Be concrete. No preamble.\n\n(End of file - total 69 lines)\n</content>","title":".tmp/add-ability-to-create-new-ideas-from-the-server-view.instructions","metadata":{"preview":"You are an implementer breaking down a feature plan into concrete coding tasks.\n\nFeature: Add ability to create new ideas from the server view\n\nPlan:\n## Plan: Add ability to create new ideas from the server web app\n\n### Overview\nAdd a \"New Idea\" form to the web app that sends a WebSocket message to a connected pipeline client, which then creates the idea locally using `FeatureFile.create()`.\n\n### Architecture Flow\n1. **Web UI** (index.html / client.html) → User fills in title, board, description\n2. **Server** (api.go) → New REST endpoint `POST /api/clients/{id}/ideas` receives the request\n3. **Server** (hub.go) → Forwards a `create_idea` WebSocket message to the connected pipeline client\n4. **Pipeline client** (server_client.py) → Receives `create_idea` message, calls `FeatureFile.create()`\n5. **Pipeline client** → Next state push reflects the new idea in the ideas stage\n\n### Implementation Steps\n\n#### 1. Server: Add `create_idea` WebSocket message type (hub.go)","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"time":{"start":1772836376442,"end":1772836376451}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"The user wants me to read a file with instructions and follow them exactly. Let me read the file first.","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":"54721351261e7eadb55108cfbd7000471780e501e10b4c51ae16a73ac0de5416"}]}}}}
